message.content:
You are the completeness critic for a reconnaissance pass over two OS-lab projects that must now be implemented from scratch.

Here are the reports produced so far:

### AREA: Project5-Device_Driver — Network driver (drivers/net.c) implementation surface
# P5 Network Driver — exhaustive survey

**Headline finding first:** `/workspace/Project6-File_System/drivers/net.c` contains a **complete, working reference implementation** of all three P5 stubs. Every supporting file is **byte-identical** between P5 and P6:

```
diff -u P5/drivers/net.h            P6/drivers/net.h            -> identical
diff -u P5/kernel/irq/irq.c         P6/kernel/irq/irq.c         -> identical
diff -u P5/drivers/plic.c           P6/drivers/plic.c           -> identical
diff -u P5/drivers/emacps/xemacps_main.c P6/.../xemacps_main.c  -> identical
diff -u P5/kernel/mm/mm.c           P6/kernel/mm/mm.c           -> identical (both stubbed)
```
Only `include/os/mm.h` differs (P6 carves `PGDIR_END 0x5f000000` out for an FS cache). So P6's `net.c` can be transplanted verbatim into P5.

Also note: this is **not** an e1000/"GigabitEthernet" register set. It is the **Xilinx Zynq PS GEM (EMACPS / Cadence macb)** driver. There is **no** `mac_send_desc`, `mac_recv_desc`, `set_sram_ctrl`, or `net_poll_mode()` function anywhere in the tree (`grep -rn "mac_send_desc\|mac_recv_desc\|set_sram_ctrl\|GigabitEthernet\|e1000"` → 0 hits). `net_poll_mode` is an **int global**, not a function.

---

## 1. `/workspace/Project5-Device_Driver/drivers/net.c` — full contents (41 lines)

